{"question": "Which joints of the robot arm make the finer movements?", "answer": "[1] The finer movements of the robot arm are made by the Wrist 1 and Wrist 2 joints.\n\n[2] The finer movements are also related to the stages in the MoveIt Task Constructor, particularly the `MoveRelative` stage, which allows for specifying a relative movement, such as in the Z direction.\n\n[3] The STOMP Planner can handle cost functions including torque limits, which can influence the finer movements of the robot arm.\n\n[4] The finer movements are part of the Pick and Place with MoveIt Task Constructor tutorial, where detailed stages are used to control the end effector's movement.\n\n[5] The finer movements are influenced by the `tcp_to_eef_mount_transform` parameter, which allows for adjusting the tool center point to the end effector mount link.\n\nBased on the documentation, the Wrist 1 and Wrist 2 joints are responsible for finer movements. [1]", "model": "qwen2.5:7b", "pipeline": "agent", "retrieval": "hybrid+rerank", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "search_docs", "args": {"query": "finer movements", "source": "all"}, "n_sources": 5}], "flags": [], "sources": [{"n": 1, "doc": "UR3e_User_Manual_en_SW5.24.pdf", "page": 17, "title": "3. Your Robot", "id": "ur_manual_en:p17:0"}, {"n": 2, "doc": "doc/tutorials/pick_and_place_with_moveit_task_constructor/pick_and_place_with_moveit_task_constructor.rst", "page": 11, "title": "Pick Stages", "id": "moveit_docs:doc/tutorials/pick_and_place_with_moveit_task_constructor/pick_and_place_with_moveit_task_constructor.rst#11:1"}, {"n": 3, "doc": "doc/examples/stomp_planner/stomp_planner_tutorial.rst", "page": 1, "title": "STOMP Planner", "id": "moveit_docs:doc/examples/stomp_planner/stomp_planner_tutorial.rst#1:0"}, {"n": 4, "doc": "doc/tutorials/planning_around_objects/planning_around_objects.rst", "page": 9, "title": "Next Step", "id": "moveit_docs:doc/tutorials/planning_around_objects/planning_around_objects.rst#9:0"}, {"n": 5, "doc": "doc/exampl